    "narrative": "For July 2, our offensive focus is anchored by **Jonathan Aranda**, who carries the highest projected score at 68.94. His matchup against Stephen Kolek is bolstered by a favorable wind forecast and a solid 0.375 xwOBA, translating to a strong platoon edge that pushes him into \"Strong\" start territory. **Bryson Stott** (63.08) and **Masyn Winn** (62.77) follow closely behind; **Masyn Winn** particularly benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost facing the struggling Hurston Waldrep. While **Cal Raleigh** (57.71) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.31) sit just below the \"Strong\" threshold due to the nature of their respective platoon splits, both remain viable options if our lineup confirms in favorable spots.\n\nThe bench remains relatively stagnant today, largely due to scheduled off-days for key contributors like **Lawrence Butler**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, and **Yainer Diaz**. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us without our primary engine for counting stats. Given the limited depth available for this slate, there were no razor-thin bench decisions; the optimizer prioritized the confirmed favorable matchups for **Bryson Stott** and the high-upside tilt for **Masyn Winn** against a soft pitcher. We are keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Cal Raleigh**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Gavin Sheets**; should those batting orders shift unfavorably, we risk further efficiency regression. We remain cautious of Roki Sasaki, whose underlying SP Skill marginally tempers the expectation for **Gavin Sheets**, despite the platoon advantage.",
